            <ArticleTitle>About Optimal Fractional Hold Circuits for Inter- sample Output Reconstruction in Sampled-data Systems.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3146-3155</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3390/s7123146</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The design of fractional order-holds (FROH) of correcting gains β ∈ [ - 1 , 1 ](potentially and possibly including zero-order-holds, ZOH with β=0, and first-order-holds,FROH with β=1) is discussed related to achieving output deviations being close withrespect to its sampled values. A squared error time- integral between the current output andits sampled values is minimized to yield the appropriate correcting gain of the FROH in ananalytic way.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
